Q: Linking Rust application with a dynamic library not in the runtime linker search path A: <p>Add line in <code>build.rs</code>. I had the similar issue. I got clue from this post, and extend this into build.rs per <a href="https://doc.rust-lang.org/cargo/reference/build-scripts.html" rel="nofollow noreferrer">https://doc.rust-lang.org/cargo/reference/build-scripts.html</a></p>
<pre><code>println!(&quot;cargo:rustc-link-arg=-Wl,-rpath,/home/shep/rust/dynlink/library&quot;);
</code></pre>
